WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.620
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.330
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.330
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.160
The young commanders stepped
onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.950
their sights set on a major victory.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.830
Any last words, old-timer?

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.540
You may be ignorant,
but you aren't without aptitude...

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.250
I could let you be my apprentice, Kan Ki.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.200
Yeah, right,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.450
you nobody.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.200
Forgive me, Gen Pou...

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.580
I let you die such a mundane death.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.250
Though I can't say these
soft-hearted things on the battlefield,

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.160
to lose someone with whom
I'd cheated death all those times...

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.370
But I won't be pining for you, Gen Pou.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.910
I'm about to pay Chin back--
with their soldiers' corpses!

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.410
General Kan Ki is amazing!

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.540
He avenged us here in the central army!

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.910
Thank God!

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:58.120
I was scared that old geezer was gonna
spring another weird tactic on us!

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.500
Bi Hei, you're <i>always</i> scared!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.830
Gen Pou...

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.700
I can't believe it.
That old coot, cut down so easily?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.500
Are they sure about this, Mou Ten?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.580
Yeah. General Kan Ki
disguised himself as a messenger

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.580
and sneaked into the main enemy camp.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.080
What?! Details! I need details!

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.700
But first,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.200
there's someplace I need to go. You come, too.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.410
"Someplace"?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.910
"Mou Ten's Proposal"

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.290
General Rin Ko.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.580
I understand how you must feel,
but please, we need a war council now.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.620
Everyone in the central army
is in an uproar over our tactics

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.160
now that we've lost the left flank.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:15.500
Please, sir--

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.870
Oh, shut up.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.750
I lost my parents to war.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:32.000
My lord saved me from the brink of starvation.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:38.120
And so I have given my all in the
service of being my lord's sword...

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.950
but it was Gen Pou who taught me
all I know of strategy.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:54.290
If Ren Pa is my father,
he was my grandfather...

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.080
second in line with a kindness I must repay.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.870
True, it was Gen Pou's misstep
that led to his execution.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:22.750
But for you to so casually tell me
you understand how I feel?

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.700
Honestly, it's irritating.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.250
Oh, I, uh... that is...

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:37.790
Don't worry. My lord is staying up
all night firming up a new strategy.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:40.700
All we need to do is follow it.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.790
Yes, sir!

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:05.330
Why'd you drag me
all the way out here, anyway?!

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:09.910
Don't be that way.
I have something important to discuss.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:15.000
Besides, aren't you worried
about the poor Gyoku Hou Force?

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.910
And how his wound is healing?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.080
Wha--

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.160
Not at <i>all</i> !

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.910
We've come to pay you a visit,
Ou Hon! We're coming in!

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.750
Oh! You seem well!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.160
What do you want?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.500
See? I toldja there's no point
worryin' about this guy!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.040
Get out of here. You're in the way.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.910
I was just leavin'!

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:49.870
Now, now... sit down, both of you.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.830
--Don't get between us.
--Don't be gettin' between us!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.540
Ou Hon, you've heard about
General Kan Ki taking down Gen Pou?

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.870
Yes.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.700
Surprising, right?

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:05.620
Not particularly.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.910
You liar!

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:14.160
He went down quickly for a man
who had you two in such a bind.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.910
Shut it! My spear was <i>this close</i>
to reachin' that old geezer!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.080
Well, it sure surprised <i>me</i> .

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.540
I'd heard General Kan Ki was
a military genius, but I never for a moment

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.080
thought he could pull off something so big.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:36.290
We three are looking upward...
and just above us is one huge wall.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:43.700
We need to think about where we go from here,
if only to get over that wall.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:57.500
This is the main camp, with the
Chin army's commanding general, Mou Gou.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:01.790
The central army to which we all belong
is positioned out in front of it.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:07.750
To our right is the right flank,
led by General Kan Ki,

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.410
and on the left, the left flank,
led by General Ou Sen.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.250
Now, the Gi army's
main camp is around here.

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.660
That's where their
commanding general Haku Ki Sai is,

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.290
and right now, Ren Pa is probably there, too.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:30.120
In front of their main camp,
and directly facing us, is their central army,

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:32.950
led by Rin Ko.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:37.200
They have their own left and right flanks, too.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.080
This is a lot of setup. Get to the point.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.410
After slaying Gen Pou,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:53.000
Kan Ki and his troops up and vanished.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Some think he's going after
the enemy's main camp...

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.200
but in fact, he's pulled back
to the rear and is quickly regrouping.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.000
Regrouping?

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:10.620
Yeah. Gen Pou hated Kan Ki,
but Kan Ki had it in for Kai Shi Bou.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:14.580
General Kan Ki's main forces
were attacked by Kai Shi Bou's army

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.500
and lost half their troops.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.120
Kai Shi Bou?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.790
The general heading up the enemy's left flank.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:28.040
Although if Kai Shi Bou's lost track
of Kan Ki, he can't be too rash.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.120
Meanwhile, on the other side of the battlefield,

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:35.790
Kyou En's right flank has entered the fray.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:40.080
I doubt Ou Sen can overcome
them the way things are now.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.040
Right, Ou Hon?

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.580
I mean... with both the right
and left flanks in a deadlock,

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.410
this battle is going nowhere fast.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:58.200
Enough right-left talk.
We're fightin' Rin Ko, smack in the middle.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:02.290
You don't know anything, do you.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:03.450
What?!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.950
You're half right, anyway, Shin.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:14.000
Yes, our problem at hand
is Rin Ko in the middle,

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:18.910
but his movements are closely tied
to those of the left and right flanks.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:19.950
Huh?

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.790
These past three days,

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:27.620
Rin Ko's central army has waited for
either flank to push back their opponent,

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.910
while they pull their punches.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.200
Since day two, our dedication to defense

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.620
has helped keep our casualties low...

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.250
but it makes sense that Rin Ko,

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:45.160
one of Ren Pa's Big Four, is holding back.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:49.160
Wait--Ou Hon, did you look into Rin Ko?

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.700
A little. I had my men question
one of our Gi captives.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:55.700
Oh, okay... figures.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:11:00.500
Hey, no fair! Don't keep me outta the loop here!

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:05.700
Ren Pa has four generals under him,
known as the Big Four.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:08.660
All of them have a history
of fighting alongside Ren Pa,

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.500
and all of them are exceptionally powerful.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:16.410
Kai Shi Bou, their leader, has chalked up
over a hundred victories

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.750
on his own--without Ren Pa.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.830
Kyou En, one of the top ten archers
in the whole Middle Kingdom,

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.870
was the hero of a state that
once confronted the land of Sho.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:36.000
He gave Ren Pa his share of trouble,
but after his state fell,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.870
Kyou En swore fealty to the man.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:42.040
Gen Pou worked as Ren Pa's
staff officer for many years.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.910
He was talented enough to serve
as commander of the whole Sho army.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.250
So that old guy was way up there!

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:57.500
Plus, Gen Pou also taught
strategy to a young Ren Pa.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.870
Ren Pa is mourning Gen Pou--

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:04.540
and that's why he'll go all-out
to win this battle.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:13.120
Finally, the man we're facing now: Rin Ko.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.870
If you knew Ren Pa's war records,
you'd understand.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:22.370
Indeed, Rin Ko is the most
dangerous of the Big Four.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.620
Whenever Ren Pa is involved in a big battle,

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.160
Rin Ko is always there,
getting decisive results.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.500
He's scarily good at breaking through ranks;

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:34.200
there's no telling how many
main army camps he's attacked.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:39.450
He even broke through General Ou Ki's
main forces and landed a blow.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:40.450
What?!

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:43.290
He actually landed a blow...

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.950
...on the mighty Ou Ki?!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.910
I get it now...

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.330
Rin Ko's definitely holdin' back.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.830
You got that right.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.120
If the enemy's left or right flank
circles behind General Mou Gou

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.160
and cuts off his escape route,

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.450
Rin Ko can waltz right in and attack.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:07.910
Do you think our central army can stop
a Rin Ko who's fighting in earnest?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.830
Frankly speaking, no.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:15.500
Yeah, I guess not.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.200
Now hang on!

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.580
What are you sayin' here?

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.410
Don't be givin' up before
the battle's even begun!

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:26.040
Kan Ki beat Gen Pou,
and we're aimin' even higher--

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.200
We got no business <i>not</i> goin' after Rin Ko!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.410
Rin Ko, who actually landed a blow
on General Ou Ki! He's way up there!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.370
I say bring it on!
We'll pay it all back in spades!

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.870
This works out great!

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:43.580
I fought with him first--
He can be one of my general's heads!

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:48.870
You can bet I'll be taking the head
of Rin Ko, one of Ren Pa's Big Four!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:53.120
And then I'll shoot up the ranks,
leavin' you two in the dust!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:56.330
Anyone can <i>talk</i> big.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.250
You're out of your depth.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.250
Say what?!

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:06.700
Here again, Shin, you're half right.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:11.700
We <i>do</i> have to kill Rin Ko,
who's aiming for Grandfather's main camp.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.830
However,

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.450
it won't be in retaliation for his attack.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.830
Mou Ten... what are you trying to say?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.290
If we can't stop a marauding Rin Ko,
maybe we can keep him from attacking.

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:34.830
In other words, we defeat him
before he can strike us.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:40.000
Tomorrow, the Gaku Ka Force,
the Gyoku Hou Force, and the Hi Shin Unit

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.250
will take out Rin Ko!

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.990
"Mou Ten"

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.080
Gaku Ka Force!

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:25.040
Our strong point is our ability to handle

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.040
both precise and cool-headed fighting

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.830
and crude and bloody brawling.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.290
The young sir, making a speech?

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.250
That's new...

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.620
And today... it'll be the latter.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.580
As you know, I'm not fond
of this kind of thing...

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.870
but we're faced with something only we can do.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:51.660
Today will be a battle most deadly!

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.500
Ah, I see... so that's what it is.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:01.830
He's got an important mission for us, huh?
It's been a while.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:05.410
Sorry, everyone... but I'm counting on you.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:25.290
Huh? What's the Gaku Ka Force
getting all worked up about?

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:31.410
Something's different about the Gaku Ka Force.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.910
So Sui...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:36.910
Sir?

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:40.160
We need to talk.

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.040
General Rin Ko!

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.120
Hmm?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.370
A message from the main camp!

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.910
The fighting's been postponed.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.620
The Gen Pou memorial battle
begins tomorrow, eh?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.660
Got it! Then shall we get started?

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:18.660
Stand firm! Keep your defense strong
and we will not fail!

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.160
Remain calm... and fight!

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:27.040
Oh, no! General Do Mon!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.200
A unit has ignored orders
and is entering the fray!

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.540
What?!

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:36.000
The Gaku Ka Force!

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.290
General Do Mon!

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.950
A message from Commander Mou Ten
of the Gaku Ka Force!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.290
"The Gaku Ka Force will henceforth
be an independent unit.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:47.160
We have left behind our post
and two hundred troops"!

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.500
They <i>what</i> ?!

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:59.660
You just saved us the trouble
of going out there to kill you!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.660
Surround him and take his head!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.910
Gaku Ka Force! To the right!

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:31.040
There's Rin Ko's main camp...

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:36.370
Rin Ko, sir, one of the enemy's units
is headed right for us!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:41.790
Whoa! Do you think they're after... me?

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:44.580
I don't <i>think</i> that was in the Chin army's plan...

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.080
If they're acting on their own,

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.080
it's practically suicide.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.080
Oh, I know.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.120
I know how hard it is

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.200
for us three rivals to join together.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.580
But if we don't, we'll fall together.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:18.080
The Gaku Ka Force can't kill Rin Ko on its own.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:21.410
The same goes for the
Gyoku Hou and Hi Shin Units.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.290
Don't be paintin' us with the same brush!

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:28.750
It's great that we've been rivals all this time,

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.540
but our situation's changed drastically.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:39.660
We've taken three castles, with the Gyoku Hou,
Gaku Ka, and Hi Shin Units

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.870
all distinguishing themselves.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:45.250
But honestly? Our fame isn't
exactly ringing through Chin,

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:49.120
much less anywhere else.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.750
And yet...

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:55.200
here we are, fighting that Ren Pa.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:59.580
Once the legendary great general
Ren Pa joined the battle,

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.250
the whole Middle Kingdom had its eyes on

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:05.080
the Sanyou Offensive's final showdown.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.700
The whole Middle Kingdom... watching us?

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:15.950
But we can't get Rin Ko like this.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:21.120
If we don't, our commanding general,
Mou Gou, is a sitting duck.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.370
If someone goes after General Mou Gou,

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:28.910
we'll lose to Ren Pa,
who's not leading the Sho army,

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:32.700
which he trained himself and can freely control,

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.080
but the Gi army he commands as an outsider.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:38.950
People'll be talking about the
world's greatest general, all right.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:52.290
I never thought I'd hear those words
come out of your mouth, Mou Ten.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.500
I guess not.

00:20:54.870 --> 00:21:00.950
I haven't been as passionate
about that as you two are.

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:06.000
But I'm a different man
this time around, Ou Hon.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.540
As I said earlier,

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.870
we can't let Mou Gou be killed.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:18.580
After all, he's my very dear Grandfather,

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:21.540
always watching over his
happy-go-lucky grandson.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:31.410
Taking your own feelings
with you onto the battlefield...

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:32.500
How absurd.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.000
It is <i>not</i> !

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:39.910
Everyone's fightin'
to protect something precious,

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:42.790
defendin' their line in the sand.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.080
All right, Mou Ten--

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.660
the Hi Shin Unit is with you.

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:57.330
We gotta tell the whole Middle Kingdom:

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:00.250
The leading role in this war
is about to be recast!

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:04.040
Well? What about you,

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:05.080
Ou Hon?

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:09.580
It depends on our strategy.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:13.540
Then let's talk strategy.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:17.700
First the Gaku Ka Force goes
after Rin Ko's main camp alone...

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:23.370
Aha... a wedge formation.

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.370
After all, they'll need a focused breakthrough

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:27.870
if they're coming after me with so few.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:30.290
Okay, Chin army--

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:33.080
show me how you can pierce these ranks!

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:38.450
Wait! So you're the only ones
who get to go take down Rin Ko?

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.040
We can't--hence our plan, remember?

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:46.910
C'mon, troops! Let's do this!

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:53.660
Focused breakthrough on the way!
Garrison, into position!

00:22:57.950 --> 00:22:58.950
Now!

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:02.450
What?!

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:07.450
Phase one of our strategy:

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:14.790
The Gaku Ka Force... will <i>not</i> go after Rin Ko!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:57.970
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"Three Forces United"
